BullMQ Lua scripts (expanded)
================================

Files in this directory:

  cleanJobsInSet.lua
  getCounts.lua
  getRanges.lua
  removeJob.lua

Origin
------

Extracted from the locked dependency in this repository:

  node_modules/.pnpm/bullmq@5.63.2/node_modules/bullmq/dist/cjs/scripts/*.js

Each file there embeds the fully expanded script (the `--- @include` directives of
`dist/cjs/commands/*.lua` resolved) as the `content` template literal. The files
here are that embedded content copied verbatim, so the requires/includes and the
function ordering are exactly what BullMQ 5.63.2 executes against Redis.

Mapping from BullMQ command names (and script versions) to file names:

  cleanJobsInSet:3   -> cleanJobsInSet.lua
  getCounts:1        -> getCounts.lua
  getRanges:1        -> getRanges.lua
  removeJob:2        -> removeJob.lua

Why the scripts are vendored
----------------------------

The NestJS BullmqQueueCleanupService calls Queue.clean(), Queue.getJobCounts(),
Queue.getJobs() and Job.remove(). Each of those resolves to the scripts above.
Re-implementing their range/lock/marker semantics in Go would drift; running the
same Lua keeps the deleted set and the surviving jobs identical to NestJS.

The Go call sites pass the same keys and argument tuples the matching BullMQ
JavaScript methods build (classes/queue.js, classes/queue-getters.js and
classes/scripts.js of the same version).

